 "section_summary": "This section (pages 1–55) contains records relating to Japanese educational institutions compiled by the Civil Information and Education Section of General Headquarters, Supreme Commander for the Allied Powers (GHQ SCAP). It begins with a regional reference map of Northern Honshu from a preceding report, followed by Special Report AR-302-E-A-26-3 (dated February 20, 1948) covering Aomori Prefecture. The report presents an introductory overview, classification charts, and comprehensive statistical tables detailing school counts, enrollments, and teaching personnel as of April and November 1946 across national, prefectural, municipal, town/village, and private jurisdictions. The remainder of the section provides an institutional roster listing individual schools in Aomori Prefecture by administrative control and educational level, concluding partway through the roster of village and town youth schools.",
